ngine/godot/issues/comments/3065213923","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/108539#issuecomment-3065213923","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/108539","id":3065213923,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc62s3Pj","user":{"login":"BielyDev","id":71566495,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNTY2NDk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71566495?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev","html_url":"https://github.com/BielyDev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BielyDev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-12T12:29:30Z","updated_at":"2025-07-12T12:29:30Z","body":"> Esse é o comportamento esperado, o `for` o Loop nunca filtra os elementos sobre os quais itera. Se a coleção encontrar um elemento do tipo \"errado\", você deverá usar a verificação de tipo e uma variável local dentro do bloco de loop:\n> \n> for node: Node in parent.get_children():\n>     if node is not Control:\n>         continue\n>     var control: Control = node\n>     # ...\n\n\n\nI ended up making a mistake in the issue title by using the word \"filter\" — what I actually expected was an error to occur when the key is not of the type specified in the for loop.\nI also edited the description to reflect the correct error in the script.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.githu